sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Archaeopteris hibernica Famennian epidermal Turing wavelength (31 µm, 370 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 84.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg kinetics on a periodic 186 µm square. gamma is solved so argmax sigma(k) is 31 µm. Seeded steady state locks that mode (numerical wavelength 31.0 µm). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9865, RMSE = 0.0375. Equal-diffusion control does not form a pattern (amplitude ratio 0.669) but the decay is shallow. An unseeded run at the same gamma selects 26.6 µm, one Fourier bin off. Gamma sweep from 0.25x to 4x shortens both the analytical and the noise-selected wavelength. The growth GIF is the NMNH frond veiled by the activator (CV similarity 96, 12 frames, 630x720). Overall 84.3/100 (faithfulness 83.3, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 465507 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 a62d6e1c484adc8fb84151e11566bf8c8d95d692a5a7597283b8b19ff1612a43 (sha256 a62d6e1c484adc8fb84151e11566bf8c8d95d692a5a7597283b8b19ff1612a43), spec_fingerprint a4e175a99a098be3c6247b8689ef9fb8b86a807901aee40d5798aca5032374bc. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a4e175a99a098be3c6247b8689ef9fb8b86a807901aee40d5798aca5032374bc; artifact_sha256: a62d6e1c484adc8fb84151e11566bf8c8d95d692a5a7597283b8b19ff1612a43; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0/Archaeopteris_hibernica_NMNH.jpg=20c480a93bc91bf3..., datasets/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=655a409a6f13bf84..., datasets/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4912199010e7d045...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Meyer-Berthaud, Scheckler and Wendt (1999) establish a planated megaphyll and modern tree habit for Archaeopteris by the Famennian. | Turing (1952) gives a diffusion-driven instability at a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the two-species kinetics used here. | Boyce and Knoll (2002) treat planation as the step that makes a laminate leaf.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma = 0.6636 so that argmax sigma(k) = 2*pi/31 per micrometre on this Jacobian. | Thickness scaling lambda(h) = 31*(h/12.4)^0.62 gives 66 µm (Tetraxylopteris) and 21 µm (Elkinsia). | The GIF multiplies the museum frond by a resized activator veil. The photograph does not resolve 31 µm cells.; transfer_boundary: An animal pigment Turing pattern is being used as the kinetics for a fossil epidermis whose original chemistry is not preserved.; does_not_claim: That 31 µm was measured on the Smithsonian slab or in the 1999 Nature paper. | That the predecessor and successor wavelengths are direct fossil measurements. | That nanopublications were signed. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Drive the equal-diffusion ablation ratio below 0.3 with a longer, still-stable control, and record that ratio.",
            "remediation needed: Keep the specimen KS, radial Pearson, and radial RMSE beside the dispersion goodness-of-fit so the frond comparison is not only the CV scalar.",
            "remediation needed: Quantify the finite-amplitude shift between the seeded 31.0 µm mode and the unseeded 26.6 µm mode in metrics.json and on the comparison figure." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.843"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

